  "title": "How one search narrows a question to directories, then to files",
  "source": "plan-proposal",
  "source_detail": "PLAN.md Q3c option b (proposed), D19 and D20 (decided)",
  "explanation": "[One round of questions](#ask) scores every router twice at once, then [the walk](#walk) goes top-down over those scores with no further waiting: go into a directory if X may be somewhere inside it, answer with it if X is in its own files. The root is entered on every search but is an answer only when X sits in its own files. Leaves out the hook and the per-repo sending switch, which sit in front of all of this.",
